<title>PERU: Andean Group to discuss Mercosur pact Sept 17.</title>
<headline>Andean Group to discuss Mercosur pact Sept 17.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Andean Group foreign ministers will meet in Lima on September 17 to discuss negotiations for a possible trade pact with the Mercosur bloc.</p>
<p>Peruvian government daily El Peruano said the meeting would emphasize the importance of negotiating in block with Mercosur, which includes Argentina, Brazil, Paraguay and Uruguay, &quot;in order to preserve the advances of integration and avoid the Andean Community losing its identity.&quot;</p>
<p>The Andean Group, which will soon change its name formally to Andean Community, has its administrative headquarters in Lima and consists of Peru, Bolivia, Ecuador, Colombia and Venezuela.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134</p>
